Rectifier diodes are fundamental components in power conversion, allowing current to flow primarily in one direction. They are used to convert alternating current to direct current, protect power paths, support freewheeling functions and manage current in electronic systems. Demand spans consumer power supplies, automotive electronics, industrial drives, telecommunications equipment and renewable-energy converters, where diode performance influences efficiency, thermal behavior and reliability.

According to SemiconductorInsight, the Rectifier Diode Market was valued at USD 4.01 billion in 2025 and is estimated to reach USD 4.11 billion in 2026. The market is projected to reach USD 4.93 billion by 2034, representing a CAGR of 2.3% during 2026–2034. Greater China is identified as the largest market in 2025, supported by large-scale electronics manufacturing and a strong regional semiconductor supply base.

